Description: Wild OS Remote
 Remote connects to other computers: Windows PCs and servers with Remote
 Desktop, and servers over SSH. Desktops are drawn by the same engine as
 Windows mode, full screen or in a window. SSH hosts open in a terminal
 with snippets and suggestions from your own history, a file view that
 copies over SFTP, and a keychain for your keys. Host identities are
 checked against known_hosts and a changed one is never accepted without
 asking. Passwords are kept only in the keyring, and only when you tick it.
